Many thanks to Brian Ripley and Hong Ooi for their quick replies.
Their comments, particular those from Brian, make me believe that
it must be my fault, and indeed it is. I forgot to change DLL_LOAD
in front of S_EVALUATOR and didn't realized it is !defined(DLL_LOAD)
not defined(DLL_LOAD), which makes the same programs usable in
