trying to do a lm() of, say,

    y ~ x1 + x2 + x3

But I want to limit the range of the estimated coefficients
b1, b2, and b3 to be nonnegative.  I suppose one way to do
this would be to do the original lm() and then take out
terms with negative coefficients.  But I'm wondering if
there is a more intelligent way to actually incorporate the
constraint into the least square fit estimation?

