I also use emacs; I use string-rectangle, which is useful
for many editing tasks, anything that requires putting the same
character, or group of characters, at the same place in multiple
lines.  To perform the reverse task, removing characters from
multiple lines, I use kill-rectangle.  I've bound these to keystrokes
for convenience; if you are a new emacs user ask me how.

I prefer the style of S+ and LaTeX, where individual lines are commented.
I've been burned by C comments, when I put comments around a block of
code that already contained a comment.

Tim Hesterberg

