Subject: SUMMARY: S-Plus 6 GUI Graphics Bugs
Message-ID: <5.1.0.14.2.20011024135429.02b28d08@nsmail.ccfhrb.noaa.gov>

My original message, titled "Selections in S-Plus 6 Graphsheet," asked if 
others had also experienced frequent crashes and other bugs in S-Plus GUI 
graphics under Windows.

I received responses from two different users.

The first user said:  "Not in S6.0 but I had similar experiences in SP2000 
and resolved then never to mess with S-Plus GUI graphics again. . . .  I 
think S-Plus command graphics capabilities are way too complex and powerful 
to be successfully invoked or emulated through a GUI. Or at least with the 
quality and quantity of programming resources Insightful can throw at it . 
. . ."

The second user said:  "Has anyone replied to your email in snews yet? I 
too am getting many stability problems using SPlus 6.0 on Windows NT.  I'm 
especially having problems with using graphics and with memory (The 
routines that do memory allocation/deallocation seem buggy.)"

I conclude from the relative scarcity of responses that one of the 
following is probably true:

(1) The crashes and bugs are configuration-specific, and don't affect most 
users.

(2) Other S-News readers don't use the GUI graphics features or don't use 
the Windows version.

(3)  Other users have experienced similar problems, but are unwilling to 
comment.

--
