From dsmith at insightful.com  Thu Oct 25 22:00:14 2001
From: dsmith at insightful.com (David Smith)
Date: Thu, 25 Oct 2001 15:00:14 -0700
Subject: Solution for instability with S-PLUS graphics
Message-ID: <LFEOLJDPHEIPIBEOGDDBMEMCDOAA.dsmith@insightful.com>

To follow on from the recent discussions, we have recently become aware of a
problem in S-PLUS 6.0 R1 and S-PLUS 6.0 R2 related to the graphics system in
S-PLUS.  This problem affects only certain versions of Windows (notably 98
and ME), and only when certain printer drivers are installed.  Details are
given below.  I've waited until now to respond because we've been QA-testing
a fix to this problem.  The testing is now complete, and the fix will be
included in S-PLUS 6.1, expected early next year.  In the meantime, if you
are experiencing instability with S-PLUS graphics as described below, a fix
is available from our support team.  See http://www.insightful.com/support/
for details on how to contact Tech Support.

Thanks to those people who reported and provided additional information
about this bug -- it was a tricky one to track down.  As a reminder, bugs in
S-PLUS can always be reported to bugs at insightful.com.

Sincerely,
# David Smith

PATCH TITLE:    Fpufix

APPLICABILITY:  S-PLUS 6.0 for Windows, Release 1 and Release 2
                      on computers running Windows 95, 98 or Windows ME
BACKGROUND:

Certain printer drivers make changes to the control vector of
computer's floating point unit and fail to restore the control
vector to its original state upon exit. In the context of S-PLUS,
this can happen when calling graphsheet() directly, or indirectly
through a plotting function. The problems may not show up
immediately, but may occur later in an S-PLUS session. Typical
symptoms may include the inability to print vectors or functions
in the Commands window, or even a General Protection Fault (GPF).
The command line may also become unresponsive in executing functions.

SOLUTION:

Contact technical support for a fix to this problem.

--
