From maitra at math.umbc.edu  Sun Oct 28 15:38:31 2001
From: maitra at math.umbc.edu (Ranjan Maitra)
Date: Sun, 28 Oct 2001 10:38:31 -0500
Subject: Re: Error in k-means clustering
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.33.0110281036360.8230-100000@param.math.umbc.edu>

The problem is that you have not enough memory. While I would be
interested in knowing whether you get any suggestions that could work
around this problem, I would be very surprised that something like
this is actually possible.

The problem of what to do when we are clustering a massive dataset has
been studied (though its importance largely overlooked, given that
clustering is by and large a statistically difficult problem) in the
literature. My own suggestion has been to cut up the dataset in
several parts (strategically, as your sample size allows) and then use
k-means. For more information, refer to my paper "Clustering Massive
Datasets with Applications to Software Metrics and Tomography" (by
Ranjan Maitra) which came out in the August 2001 Special Tukey
Memorial Issue of Technometrics. The paper needs the assumption of
Gaussian clusters with equal dispersion matrices to proceed. I am
currently extending the algorithm to more general cases.  

May I ask you about your dataset? Is it publicly available? What are
the data on?

Thanks,
Ranjan

