Dear S-plus friends,

I have a large dataframe and would like to subset dataset A according to a 
variable b1 in another dataset B in an efficient way. A simplified example:

A.df <- data.frame(c("one", "two", "one", "three"), c(45, 0, 8, 89))
names(A.df) <- c("a1", "a2")
> A.df
     a1 a2 
1   one 45
2   two  0
3   one  8
4 three 89

B.df <- data.frame(c("one", "two"), c(1, 2))
names(B.df) <- c("b1", "b2")
> B.df
   b1 b2 
1 one  1
2 two  2

now subset A.df via variable a1 for B.df$b1 which should result in Akeep.df

> Akeep.df
   a1 a2 
1 one 45
2 two  0
3 one  8

In principle one could use

Akeep.df<-A.df[A.df$a1=="one" | A.df$a1=="two", ]

but in my case the dataset B.df has many factor levels in variable b1 so it 
will be difficult to manually compose the OR comparator. Who would have a 
suggestion for an efficient subscription procedure?

Thank you very much in advance

Best regards

> Ansgar
