Hi List,

This is the summary of a question I asked about 10 days or so ago. As
usual, I received a very effective solution.

My original question follows,

the solution I used was from Dr. Harrell's deisgn library. Thank you Dr.
Harrell.

attach(dataset)
dd <- datadist(variable names, q.display(0, 1), q.effects(0, 1))
options(datadist = "dd")
model.lrm <- lrm(May.cat ~ VAR1 + VAR2  etc.)
plot(model.lrm, fun=plogis, ylab="Probability", ylim=c(0, 1),
conf.int=0.95)

This gives me exactly what I wanted, a plot of predicted probability
with confidence intervals for values of each independent variable. The
values of the other independent variables are adjusted to their
respective medians.
