On the contrary, logically we still can use this model. You've got to be 
careful though not to overfit it with extraneous quadratic terms which 
can inflate the variance of estimates and reduce power of the tests 
dramatically. The multicollinearity should be taken care of by means of 
any standard procedures, say PROC REG in SAS package provides tools for 
that. As to multicollinearity condition (a.k.a. multiple correlation in 
the design matrix), it can come up anywhere anytime even with model with
linear terms only.

